    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a condensed lineup as heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are sidelined by team off-days. With fewer high-end starters available, **Sam Antonacci** emerges as our strongest play. His score of 63.61 is driven by the premium leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Rocker, whose 4.36 xERA provides a clear window for production. While **Miguel Vargas** also draws Rocker, his score of 55.00 is dampened slightly by a negative park factor, though he remains a solid play due to his consistent presence in the three-hole and a strong 0.389 xwOBA.\n\nThe most intriguing value play is **Nasim Nunez**, who grades out at a 59.76. Despite batting ninth, **Nasim Nunez** benefits immensely from facing Feltner, whose 5.10 xERA is the most exploitable on the board today. The high SP skill benefit (+19%) keeps him ahead of **Jackson Merrill**, whose 51.66 score reflects a much tougher assignment against Ashcraft. We are monitoring **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Jordan Westburg** closely as they occupy our high-leverage bench spots; they remained out of the primary rotation today only because their current matchups offer less upside for stolen base accumulation compared to the efficiency profile of **Sam Antonacci**. We remain cautious with **Jackson Merrill** given his -18% penalty against Ashcraft\u2019s specific arm profile, but the depth of our roster\u2014including prospects like **Tommy White** and **Luis Lara**\u2014ensures we have enough flexibility to pivot if mid-game reports indicate unfavorable wind shifts.",
